---
/* Four things worth knowing about IOP,
   ordered by how often they come up in our own admissions calls. */
const questions = [
  {
    q: 'Can I keep working?',
    a: "Keeping a job is one of the main reasons IOP exists at all. Our schedules are built to flex around work, school and family, so treatment fits into the week rather than replacing it. Tell admissions what your week actually looks like and they will work the timing out with you on the call.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there housing with it?',
    a: "Often what somebody needs is not just the program but somewhere steady to live while they attend it. We do not run sober living ourselves, but placement help is part of this phase: we know the local landscape and our case managers line the two up together.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Will my insurance cover it?',
    a: "Usually some of it, but outpatient care is often contracted separately from inpatient, so a plan that covers a residential stay will not automatically cover IOP at the same rate. It is worth knowing before you start rather than after. We will run your benefits with you on the phone.",
  },
  {
    q: "I just finished residential. What's next?",
    a: "Stepping down into PHP or IOP is the standard next move, and it is also where momentum is easiest to lose, because nobody handed over the next appointment. Here that handover happens inside one building, with the case manager you already know setting it up before your discharge date.",
  },
];
---
<section id="iop-questions" class="bg-white py-[70px]">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <p class="text-gold font-body text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="w-6 h-px bg-gold inline-block"></span>
      Worth knowing
    </p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-charcoal mb-10">
      Four things worth knowing about IOP
    </h2>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      {questions.map(item => (
        <div class="bg-cream rounded-xl p-7 border border-cream-soft">
          <h3 class="q-title font-display text-navy mb-3">{item.q}</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-charcoal text-[16px] leading-[27px]">{item.a}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Unlayered, so it beats the global h3 scale. */
  .q-title { font-size: 24px; line-height: 30px; letter-spacing: 0; }
</style>
